363	<section id="designs">
364	  <h2><span class="num">4</span>The two designs</h2>
365	  <p class="gist">Both keep the shape: workers, a checker per rung or pair, one repair round, a merge, one gate. They differ in the checking and in the tail.</p>
366	
367	  <div class="sub" id="fable">
368	    <h3>The Fable design</h3>
369	    <p class="before"><b>Before the launch</b> the coordinator builds the base once, about 4 minutes, and puts each rung's section of the record into the run's arguments <span class="src">Fable §2</span>. <b>Order:</b> C, W, N, G, two at a time <span class="src">Fable §1</span>.</p>
370	    <ol class="roles">
371	      <li>
372	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Worker</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span><span class="count">×4</span></div>
373	        <p>Its brief is its rung's section of the record, with no separate briefing. Tests first, committed alone. Then one suite run, chosen by what the edit can break: W runs <code>testSystem</code>; C runs the compiler and library tracks of <code>testFast</code>; G and N run only their own tests, which load the whole library. C, G and N run the two stages once at the end. It writes the ledger, FACTS and PLAN lines into its report, not into those files.</p>
374	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>2.5M to 3.3M</b> <span class="src">Fable §4</span></p>
375	      </li>
376	      <li>
377	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Skeptic</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span><span class="count">×4</span></div>
378	        <p>Reads the git log, the diff, the report and the tool lines of the worker's transcript. Runs 3 to 6 programs of its own on new and old code. Builds nothing. It may refuse only on six listed grounds <span class="src">Fable §2</span>:</p>
379	        <ul>
380	          <li>a test not seen failing first, or not committed alone;</li>
381	          <li>a stop of the brief met and not listed;</li>
382	          <li>a fix against the text or library practice the brief cites;</li>
383	          <li>a file touched outside the brief's list;</li>
384	          <li>a value changed without the brief's warrant;</li>
385	          <li>a test that cannot fail for the reason it names.</li>
386	        </ul>
387	        <p>Anything else is a note for you.</p>
388	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.8M to 1.2M</b>, 0.2M to 0.3M each <span class="src">Fable §4</span></p>
389	      </li>
390	      <li>
391	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">After a refusal</span><span class="count">one chain expected</span></div>
392	        <ul>
393	          <li><span class="tier opus">Opus</span> <b>Repair</b> of exactly the named grounds: 0.3M.</li>
394	          <li><span class="tier opus">Opus</span> <b>Second read</b>, of those grounds only: 0.15M.</li>
395	          <li><span class="tier opus">Opus</span> <b>Ruling</b>, only if the second read refuses again, approve or drop: 0.15M.</li>
396	          <li><span class="tier fable">Fable</span> <b>Second ruling</b>, only if the Opus ruling says the dispute is a design question across two of the specification, the library and the implementation: 0.15M, rarely.</li>
397	        </ul>
398	        <p>A rung not approved stays on its branch; the batch lands without it.</p>
399	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.6M</b> a chain; one expected, two budgeted <span class="src">Fable §4</span></p>
400	      </li>
401	      <li>
402	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Gather</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span></div>
403	        <p>Merges the approved branches with merge commits in a seeded worktree, and writes the records from the workers' reports.</p>
404	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.25M</b> <span class="src">Fable §4</span></p>
405	      </li>
406	      <li>
407	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Gate</span><span class="tier sonnet">Sonnet, low effort</span></div>
408	        <p>One build of the merged tree, then <code>testFast</code>, <code>testSystem</code>, the ladder, the count and the distance, one after another. A red gate gets one Opus repair and one more gate.</p>
409	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.10M to 0.15M</b>; a red gate adds 0.4M and 0.1M, expected once in three batches <span class="src">Fable §4</span></p>
410	      </li>
411	      <li>
412	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Landing</span><span class="tier sonnet">Sonnet, low effort</span></div>
413	        <p>Writes the gate's numbers into the landing note, fast-forwards <code>main</code>, pushes, starts the microGPT runs.</p>
414	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.08M</b> <span class="src">Fable §4</span></p>
415	      </li>
416	    </ol>
417	    <p class="note">Not in it: the merged-diff review, and a judge on every refusal <span class="src">Fable §1</span>.</p>
418	    <div class="total">
419	      <p><b>Estimate:</b> about 5.2M (4.3M to 6.8M), including about 0.25M of the coordinator's own work outside the run. 11 to 19 agents, 13 to 14 expected. About 9 to 10 hours <span class="src">Fable §4</span>.</p>
420	    </div>
421	  </div>
422	
423	  <div class="sub" id="opus">
424	    <h3>The Opus design</h3>
425	    <p class="before"><b>Before the launch</b> the coordinator builds or reuses the base build, renders each rung's briefing, and commits two small tools: <code>gate.sh</code>, the gate's steps as one script, and <code>test-first-trace.py</code>, which prints a worker's test runs from its transcript <span class="src">Opus §2, §5</span>. <b>Order:</b> C, N, G, W, two at a time <span class="src">Opus §1</span>.</p>
426	    <ol class="roles">
427	      <li>
428	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Worker</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span><span class="count">×4</span></div>
429	        <p>Its rung's section plus its briefing. Tests first, committed alone; the fix; the text in the S1 form. One <i>reach run</i>, the part of the suite its change can reach: <code>testFast</code> for C, <code>testSystem</code> for W, N and G. C, N and G run the two stages once. New ledger rows get placeholders that the integrator numbers.</p>
430	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>2.25M</b> (1.8M to 2.75M) <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
431	      </li>
432	      <li>
433	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Checker</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span><span class="count">×3</span></div>
434	        <p>One for W, one for C, and one for N and G together. Checks test first from git and the transcript, the paths touched, each fix against its text or precedent, at most eight programs of its own, the worker's results, and the revised text <span class="src">Opus §2</span>. It may commit text-only corrections. It approves unless a code or test finding stands on a program or a cited line.</p>
435	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.88M</b> (0.69M to 1.12M) <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
436	      </li>
437	      <li>
438	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">After a refusal</span><span class="count">1.4 expected</span></div>
439	        <ul>
440	          <li><span class="tier opus">Opus</span> <b>Repair</b>: accepts each finding, turning the checker's program into a test that fails first and then fixing it, or contests it with evidence. About 0.28M each, 0.43M expected.</li>
441	          <li><span class="tier fable">Fable</span> <b>Ruling</b>, only for a contested finding: one ruling, final. About 0.15M each, 0.05M expected.</li>
442	          <li><span class="tier opus">Opus</span> <b>Second repair</b>, only after an upheld ruling: 0.04M expected.</li>
443	        </ul>
444	        <p>No second skeptic.</p>
445	        <p class="cost">Estimates <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
446	      </li>
447	      <li>
448	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Integrator</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span></div>
449	        <p>Merges with merge commits into a fresh, unseeded worktree, numbers the rows, starts <code>gate.sh</code> in the background (a clean build and the full gate, 25 to 35 minutes <span class="src">Opus §2</span>), and writes the records while it runs. Pushes a work branch, never <code>main</code>.</p>
450	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.28M</b> <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
451	      </li>
452	      <li>
453	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Reviewer</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span><span class="count">beside the integrator</span></div>
454	        <p>Reads the four diffs side by side for what no single check could see. Its text corrections land before the push. Its code findings become rows for the next batch and block nothing.</p>
455	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.25M</b> <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
456	      </li>
457	      <li>
458	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Gate repair</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span><span class="count">red gate only</span></div>
459	        <p>Repairs the merged tree as a whole, then one more gate.</p>
460	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.1M</b> expected (0.4M at a 0.25 chance) <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
461	      </li>
462	      <li>
463	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Lander</span><span class="tier opus">Opus, low effort</span></div>
464	        <p>Applies the review's text corrections, checks that no gated path changed since the gate, pushes <code>main</code>, starts the microGPT runs.</p>
465	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.08M</b> <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
466	      </li>
467	      <li>
468	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Measure</span><span class="tier sonnet">Sonnet, low effort</span></div>
469	        <p>Measures the run's cost by role from its journal and writes it beside this estimate.</p>
470	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.1M</b> <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
471	      </li>
472	    </ol>
473	    <div class="total">
474	      <p><b>Estimate:</b> about 4.3M on Opus (3.0M to 6.4M), up to 0.2M on Fable, about 0.1M on Sonnet. 10 Opus agents and the measure in the base case, about 12 expected, 17 at worst. About 9.5 to 10 hours (8 to 12) <span class="src">Opus §4</span>.</p>
475	    </div>
476	  </div>
