615	<section id="tokens">
616	  <h2><span class="num">6</span>Where the tokens go today</h2>
617	  <p class="gist">A Sonnet measurement of batches 8 and 9 on the existing pipeline: 43 agents, 14.60M written <span class="src">Labor</span>.</p>
618	  <ul>
619	    <li><b>The fixed start.</b> Every agent starts with 69K to 108K tokens of context before it does anything: the system prompt and tools, the harness's attachments, and its brief. Written across both batches, that is 2.84M, 19.5% of everything <span class="src">Labor</span>. The 45K floor the designers were given <span class="src">Brief</span> is the part before the brief, about 42K; today's briefs add 27K to 56K by role <span class="src">Labor</span>.</li>
620	    <li><b>Thinking.</b> The agents' own thinking and narration is the largest single class: 3.92M, 26.9%. Whether it was all needed cannot be measured <span class="src">Labor</span>.</li>
621	    <li><b>Checking against building.</b> Roles whose job is to check or judge hold 6.26M, 42.9% of the writes. Rung workers hold 36.7%. The refusal cycle (judge, repair, second skeptic) is 3.34M, 22.9%, because both batches refused two rungs <span class="src">Labor</span>.</li>
622	    <li><b>Exploring beyond the brief.</b> Little, and mostly by searching. A rung worker reads 54K of its 536K (10%) beyond what its brief names. 74% of the files it opens beyond the brief are named in its briefing, FACTS or the maps. No agent opened <code>INDEX.md</code> <span class="src">Labor</span>.</li>
623	    <li><b>Reading a later agent repeats.</b> 1.39M of 4.73M read (29%) were lines an earlier agent of the same batch had already been given. In a chain the followers repeat 750K of 1.77M (42%); the tail repeats 398K of 1.28M (31%). Much of this is the checking itself: an agent that does not look at the diff cannot check it. So 750K is a ceiling, not a saving <span class="src">Labor</span>.</li>
624	  </ul>
625	
626	  <div class="sub">
627	    <h3>The eight levers, saving per batch</h3>
628	    <p class="note">They overlap, and the measurement recommends none of them <span class="src">Labor</span>.</p>
629	    <ol class="levers">
630	      <li><b>Let the cache share the identical start.</b> 0.15M to 0.24M with today's 5-minute cache; 0.74M to 0.91M with a one-hour cache or a keep-warm call.
631	        <span class="lever-cost">Needs a harness feature; whether the Workflow tool offers one is unknown <span class="src">Labor</span>.</span></li>
632	      <li><b>Several reads in one turn</b> instead of one read a turn. 0.30M to 0.40M.
633	        <span class="lever-cost">Untested: it assumes the thinking between reads goes away <span class="src">Labor</span>.</span></li>
634	      <li><b>The review fixes a text-only finding itself</b>, without a judge and a repair. 0.3M to 0.35M when it recurs, as it did in both batches.
635	        <span class="lever-cost">Risk: in batch 9 the judge found two errors in the review's own proposed sentence <span class="src">Labor</span>.</span></li>
636	      <li><b>The gate as a script</b>, with an agent only on failure. 0.12M to 0.24M.
637	        <span class="lever-cost">A flaky stage or a failure still needs a model. The Opus design's <code>gate.sh</code>, started by the integrator, takes this route <span class="src">Labor</span> <span class="src">Opus §2</span>.</span></li>
638	      <li><b>Chain followers read only the briefing the worker had not.</b> 0.07M to 0.12M.
639	        <span class="lever-cost">Weakens the skeptic's independent check against the record <span class="src">Labor</span>.</span></li>
640	      <li><b>A shorter shared prefix for roles that do not need the worker's rules.</b> 0.03M to 0.06M.
641	        <span class="lever-cost">Works against lever 1, which wants one identical block <span class="src">Labor</span>.</span></li>
642	      <li><b>The gather leaves the review a digest.</b> At most 0.07M.
643	        <span class="lever-cost">The high-risk lever: the review exists to check the gather <span class="src">Labor</span>.</span></li>
644	      <li><b>File and line anchors in the brief</b> for the searches. All search is up to 0.36M; if a fifth of it goes, 0.07M.
645	        <span class="lever-cost">The anchors go stale after the first edit <span class="src">Labor</span>.</span></li>
646	    </ol>
647	  </div>
